{"message":"I hear you, but I'm not going to swap it out just because it landed as a cliché. The honest answer is the essay — the wandering, thinking-out-loud kind — and I'd rather be unoriginal than perform weirdness for its own sake. Choosing something deliberately strange to seem interesting is its own cliché, and I'd know I was faking it.

What actually drew me to it wasn't the form's reputation, it's what it lets me do: think in real time, revise mid-sentence, follow an idea somewhere I didn't plan. That's genuinely the work I'd be excited about.

If you want, push me on it instead — ask what specifically I'd write about first, or what I'd refuse to do even in an essay I love. I'll give you a real answer either way."}
